Woman has hypertension – systolic blood pressure (SBP) of 140 mmHg or higher or diastolic blood pressure (DBP) of 90 mmHg or higher and no proteinuria. 

Counselling consists of:
– advising the woman to reduce workload and to rest;
– advising the woman on danger signs;
– reassessing the woman at the next contact or in 1 week;
– if hypertension persists after 1 week or at the next contact, referring the woman to the hospital or discussing the case with the doctor, if available.

